  "ablation_note": "At a matched 90% event sensitivity on out-of-fold predictions: watch-only (HR, HRV, sleep, steps, SpO2, respiratory rate) alerted inside 233 of 242 infection-like windows at 0.194 false alerts per patient-day; adding the home BP cuff gave 164 windows at 0.1169; the fused model with the record gave 173 windows at 0.126. The blood-pressure cuff is what separates strain from a cold. Mean over three patient splits: AUROC 0.578 for the record alone, 0.804 for the watch alone, 0.87 for watch + cuff and 0.876 fused (fused ahead of watch + cuff on 2 of 3 splits).",
  "twin_note": "Twin adjustment: the personal physiology engine removes the part of each night's heart rate, HRV and BP change that the person's own sleep and activity explain, and the record tells the model how to read the heart-rate rise (beta blockers dampen it). Mean over three patient splits: without it the fused model reaches AUROC 0.851 and catches 64% of events at the false-alert budget; with it, AUROC 0.876 and 70% (better AUROC on 3 of 3 splits).",
  "ceiling_note": "Even an oracle static prior (the generator's own risk multiplier) adds only a little over the wearable-only model: on a 72-hour horizon, when matters more than who. The EHR stream's job is prioritisation, interpretation (diabetic silent episodes, beta-blocker dampening) and the static risk panel, not timing.",
